From d0a69ef3d16c05a655253499606803fd592b776e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 07:28:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Require the transaction PIN server-side on every money-moving
 endpoint

CRITICAL security fix. Every purchase endpoint (data, airtime, result
pins, and all 9 NIN/BVN verification endpoints) relied ENTIRELY on the
client showing a PIN dialog before calling them - PinConfirmDialog.tsx /
pin_confirmation_sheet.dart called POST /user/pin/verify, which genuinely
checked the PIN, but that check was never linked to the purchase call
that followed it. Nothing server-side stopped a request from skipping
the dialog and hitting e.g. POST /data/purchase directly with a valid
auth token and no PIN at all.

Backend (src/lib/require-pin.ts):
- requirePinConfirmation(userId, pin) - reuses the existing verifyPin()
  (same rolling-window lockout already used by /user/pin/verify: 5 wrong
  PINs locks for 30 minutes). A wrong PIN sent straight to a purchase
  endpoint now counts against the same lockout as one entered through the
  dialog.
- pinField - a  zod schema fragment,
  spread into every affected endpoint's body schema.
- Added to all 11 money-moving endpoints: POST /data/purchase,
  /airtime/purchase (vtu.routes.ts), /:exam/pin (result.routes.ts), and
  all 9 in verification.routes.ts (nin/by-nin, nin/by-phone,
  nin/by-demographic, bvn/slip, delinking, nin-validation,
  personalization, bvn-retrieval, ipe-clearance).
- vtu.routes.ts's two endpoints also stop spreading the raw request body
  (which now includes ) into Transaction.metadata - the pin field is
  stripped explicitly before that spread, so it can never end up
  persisted in the database.
- require-pin.test.ts (8 tests) - propagates verifyPin's INVALID_PIN /
  PIN_LOCKED / PIN_NOT_SET untouched, pinField's validation. Full backend
  suite: 79/79 passing.

Flutter (pin_confirmation_sheet.dart + 27 call-site files):
- showPinConfirmationSheet now returns Future<String?> (the verified PIN
  itself) instead of Future<bool> - every caller must include it in the
  purchase request that follows.
- Removed the biometric shortcut from this sheet specifically - a
  biometric match has nothing to send the server as the verified secret
  (the app only ever stores a one-way HASH of the PIN locally, so a
  reversible plain PIN is never sitting on-device to retrieve after
  biometric success). Biometric app-unlock elsewhere in the app
  (login_pin_unlock_screen.dart) is unaffected - only this
  money-moving-confirmation sheet now always requires the PIN to be typed.
  SecureScreenMixin (screenshot blocking while the PIN is on screen) is
  unchanged.
- Updated every real call site across all 4 clean-architecture layers
  where applicable (datasource -> repository -> notifier -> screen):
  buy_data, buy_airtime, result checker (WAEC/NECO/NABTEB, shared widget),
  all 8 verification screens (shared verification_provider.dart covers
  all 9 methods), and major_ai_assistant_screen.dart's chat-driven
  purchase flow - same endpoints as the regular screens, so this backend
  fix protects both automatically.
- Also fixed the 6 UI-only screens with no live backend yet (cable_tv,
  electricity, jamb, bulk_sms, recharge_card, airtime_to_cash) just to
  keep the app compiling under the new return type - noted these don't
  call working endpoints yet, so they weren't a live security gap.

Web (PinConfirmDialog.tsx + 4 call-site files):
- onVerified now receives the confirmed PIN string, not just a signal.
- Updated BuyDataPage.tsx, BuyAirtimePage.tsx, VerificationPage.tsx
  (one shared submit() handles all verification types), and
  MajorAssistant.tsx's purchase flow.
- Full app still type-checks and builds clean (tsc -b && vite build).
